ondary_6"}, {"content": "Writes simple but clear texts describing or reviewing places to visit in the region, using an appropriate range of vocabulary and grammatical structures.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Writes simple but clear texts describing or reviewing places to visit in the region, using an appropriate range of vocabulary and grammatical structures.", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "drive-in", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a place where people can watch movies outdoors while sitting in their cars", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I want to go to the drive-in across from the park.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn3le01ob08aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "These are words you hear about places in a city.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to go jogging", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to run as a form of exercise ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Some people prefer to go jogging on the boardwalk for exercise.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn3le01ob08aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to do yoga", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to practice yoga; to take a yoga class ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I like to do yoga on a Saturday morning in the park.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn3le01ob08aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to watch movies ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to see a film", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I like to watch movies at the theater.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn3le01ob08aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to go salsa dancing", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to do a dance that is from South America at a club or venue ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Want to go salsa dancing?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn3le01ob08aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"content": "engenn3le01ob08re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Descriptive Writing / Paragraphs ", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "Descriptive paragraphs can describe things to do in your city. You use Infinitives to make writing more descriptive and interesting to read. ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "Topic sentence:  Cambridge is a small town but there is so much to do.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "To write a descriptive paragraph you need:<br /> <br />A topic:<br /><li> the person, place, or thing you want to write about<br/></li><li>the opinion or observation that you will develop and support in the body sentences</li>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Supporting Sentences: <br/><li>background information to support your topic</li><li>descriptive details to develop your topic</li>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Concluding Sentence: <br/><li>summarize the idea in a different way </li><li>use words like <span class=\"italic\">in conclusion</span>, <span class=\"italic\">all in all</span>, or <span class=\"italic\">in summary</span> to signal the ending", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Supporting Sentence: I like to go the galleries and museums on James Blvd.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Concluding Sentence: I love living in Cambridge.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Present Simple Tense for Descriptions", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "We use the Present Simple to talk about actions that happen again and again.  </br>We use the Present Simple to talk about things that are true all the time.</br>We use the Present Simple to talk about feelings and thoughts.</br>We use the Present Simple in the interrogative form to ask questions.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "Cambridge is a wonderful place to live.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Salsa lessons are on Friday nights.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I love this city.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Do you like Cambridge?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Is there a lot to do in Cambridge?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "What is your favorite part of the city?", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Do research on a city. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Find 5 attractions you can talk about.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Choose 5 adjectives to describe the attractions.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Write a paragraph.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Share your paragraph with a partner.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Read your paragraph aloud.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I start with a topic sentence in a paragraph.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I use descriptive words.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I use supporting sentences in a paragraph about a city.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I finish with a concluding sentence in a paragraph about a city.", "type": "text"}]}], "type": "sena"}